      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, micro-interactions like humor or well-timed remarks can often de-escalate tension by injecting a moment of levity into a charged situation. They help to humanize interactions, remind participants of shared experiences, and create a more relaxed atmosphere, which can be particularly valuable in preventing small disputes from escalating into more severe conflicts.",
      "source": "target",
